WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.480
First question: I enjoy
meeting new people.

2
00:00:03.530 --> 00:00:06.440
Strongly agree, or strongly disagree?

3
00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:07.270
Tick.

4
00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:09.520
A marker slides along a bar.

5
00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:14.610
Then another question, and another,
until 16 bars are filled in.

6
00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:17.260
The finished profile
is held up next to her.

7
00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:19.260
Every bar has its dot.

8
00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:20.510
Job done?

9
00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:25.510
So can a questionnaire really capture
who you are in sixteen numbers?

10
00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:29.760
In this mission, you'll see the difference
between sorting people into types and

11
00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:31.670
measuring them on traits.

12
00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:36.370
You'll find out how a personality
scale turns your answers into scores.

13
00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:40.570
And you'll meet a questionnaire
built on 16 personality factors,

14
00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:45.480
each a scale between two
opposites, like reserved to warm.

15
00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:50.360
Your mission: decide whether sixteen
numbers can really capture who you are.
